    <title>Daily Digest 2026-09-25: Professional skepticism is a dev’s best skill; Infinidash: AWS’s New Observability Play Has Great; Chroma and Agentic Retrieval</title>
    <updated>2026-09-25T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-09-25.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Professional skepticism is a dev’s best skill&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/09/25/professional-skepticism-is-a-dev-s-best-skill/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Infinidash: AWS’s New Observability Play Has Great Bones and a Terrible Bedside Manner&lt;/b&gt; — Better visibility into your systems — new tooling or standards that reduce MTTR. &lt;a href="https://www.lastweekinaws.com/blog/cloudwatch-omni-infinidash-review/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chroma and Agentic Retrieval&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/podcasts/chroma-and-agentic-retrieval/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: A single-use authorization boundary in Rust&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49840686"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Jevper – an LLM API client constrained to the Jev wire format&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://github.com/zhulinchng/jevper"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: A benchmark comparison of C++ vs. Node.js performance&lt;/b&gt; — Benchmarks cut through the hype — useful for choosing which model or tool to actually rely on. &lt;a href="https://vikky2810.github.io/blog/cpp-vs-node/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fragments: September 24&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/fragments/2026-09-24.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Observability Day: Where the community comes together at KubeCon + CloudNativeCon North America 2026&lt;/b&gt; — Better visibility into your systems — new tooling or standards that reduce MTTR. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/09/24/observability-day-where-the-community-comes-together-at-kubecon-cloudnativecon-north-america-2026/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Introducing MentalHealthBench&lt;/b&gt; — Benchmarks cut through the hype — useful for choosing which model or tool to actually rely on. &lt;a href="https://openai.com/index/introducing-mentalhealthbench"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
